AI Design

The project intentionally avoids using an LLM for every user interaction.

Instead:

                 ┌─────────────────────┐
                 │ LLM Batch Pipeline  │
                 └──────────┬──────────┘
                            │
                    Generate once
                            │
                            ▼
                 ┌─────────────────────┐
                 │ Stored Hints +      │
                 │ Explanations        │
                 └──────────┬──────────┘
                            │
                     Used repeatedly
                            │
                            ▼
                 ┌─────────────────────┐
                 │     Web Client      │
                 └─────────────────────┘

This provides:

Lower inference cost
Predictable latency
Offline gameplay
Deterministic behavior
Consistent coaching quality
Evaluation

The generated coaching content is validated against the underlying puzzle solution.

Evaluation includes:

Puzzle correctness
Legal move validation
Solution sequence validation
FEN consistency
AI content
Explanation references the correct tactical idea
Suggested moves correspond to the actual solution
No hallucinated board positions
Structured output validation
User experience

Track:

Puzzle completion rate
Accuracy
Average attempts
Hint usage
Average solve time
Performance by tactical theme
Development
Prerequisites
Node.js
npm
Python
Lichess puzzle dataset
LLM API access for the offline content-generation pipeline
Running the Web App
npm install
npm run dev

The application will start a local development server.

Running the Puzzle Pipeline
python pipeline/download.py
python pipeline/filter.py
python pipeline/generate_coaching.py
python pipeline/validate.py

The pipeline:

Downloads the Lichess dataset
Filters and selects puzzles
Generates AI coaching content
Validates the generated dataset
Produces the application-ready puzzle database
Project Goals

This project is intended to demonstrate several engineering concepts:

Building a production-style web application
Processing a large public dataset
Deterministic state validation
Offline-first application architecture
Batch LLM inference
Structured LLM outputs
AI evaluation and validation
Adaptive user experiences
Separating probabilistic AI components from deterministic business logic
Future Improvements
